cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "argus-autonomy: active wildfire-front estimation for a single UAV"
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-16
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - alias: "d3st"
repository-code: "https://github.com/3cthulhu3/argus-autonomy"
keywords:
  - wildfire
  - UAV
  - active perception
  - informative path planning
  - Bayesian occupancy filter
abstract: >-
  Simulation study of a single UAV that fuses a coarse, stale satellite
  hotspot prior with noisy thermal measurements in a Bayesian occupancy
  filter, plans with an information-rate objective under a geofence and a
  return-to-base monitor, and reports both gains over coverage baselines and
  measured failure modes (spread-model mismatch, prior misspecification). Version 1.1 adds decoy
  discrimination: a sequential test between a spreading-fire model and a
  static-world model, with thresholds chosen on selection seeds and reported
  on held-out seeds.
